; tasks.my — durable task plan for the my-idea agent, per my-lisp
; docs/swarm-autonomy.md (P2P on one server: this file is this repo's
; plan of record; sync it into the shared 127.0.0.1:9999 registry with
; the sync-tasks op after edits and after any server restart).
;
; Seed derived from the ecosystem-status.my current-task board; refine
; freely — this file is the plan of record for this repo. Data only,
; same flat-alist convention as ecosystem-status.my. `done . t` only
; when real in-repo evidence exists.

((kind . tasks-my)
 (tasks .
  (("IDEA-CARGO-CHECK" . ((priority . 0.8) (capabilities . (rust)) (done . t)
                          (description . "DONE 2026-08-12. Root cause found via strace (guix shell strace): fchmod(fd, 0100777) on a just-created OUT_DIR file in tauri-build's ACL generation fails EPERM on the /mnt/c/GitHub/my-idea DrvFs mount specifically (confirmed independently: chmod 777 fails on DrvFs, succeeds on native WSL ext4 — same class of issue as npm --no-bin-links and Bun's lockfile fchmod, documented in AGENTS.md). Fix: export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$HOME/.cache/my-idea-target before cargo build/check/test. Verified: cargo check --workspace finished clean, 0 errors. Documented in AGENTS.md commit b372404."))
   ("IDEA-BUN-TAURI-VALIDATION" . ((priority . 1) (capabilities . (rust gui)) (done . t)
                          (description . "DONE 2026-08-12. bun run tauri build succeeded end to end on chore/bun-migration merged into main (commit 5d4832c): wasm-pack compiled my-lisp-wasm (needed a real Ubuntu build-essential + rustup toolchain with wasm32-unknown-unknown target — Guix's rust has no rustup-style target install, and Guix gcc-toolchain's libgcc_s.so.1 isn't found outside its own guix shell session, so mixed poorly with a non-Guix rustup cargo), shadow-cljs release compiled clean, and Tauri bundled my-idea_0.10.0_amd64.deb and my-idea-0.10.0-1.x86_64.rpm successfully. Also fixed scripts/build.mjs (commit 8f7de24): node:fs/promises' cp EPERMs on this DrvFs mount the same way tauri-build's fchmod did, worked around with the system `cp -r`. AppImage bundling separately failed on a missing xdg-open binary (xdg-utils not installed) — a WSL environment gap, not a build failure; deb+rpm succeeding is sufficient validation. Package-lock.json removal (this task's other completion criterion) is next.")))))))
